# Celebgate (2014). Fake cloud-account security emails collected passwords; private photo backups were downloaded.
# A quest (QUESTS.md): the trainee is an agency assistant who approves photo proofs, does one safely, then meets the fake "account locked" email.
# The 2014 victims were mostly actors and models. The agency, the assistant and the actor here are invented.
os macos
user Dana Okafor
about
  | Celebgate began with emails that looked like the cloud provider's security team and said an account was locked. The sign-in page behind the link was a copy, and it collected the passwords.
  | With a password, the attackers downloaded a full phone backup, private photos included. The owner saw nothing happen on their own screen.
story
  | You are Dana Okafor, assistant at Northwind Talent, a small agency. You look after the publicity photos of the actor Jules Marlowe.
  | It is mid-afternoon. Priya, the publicist, shares the headshot proofs into your own cloud account, one at a time. You have approved 4 of today's 6. Two to go.
  | The same account backs up your phone, private photos included. Your sign-in details are in a text file on the desktop. That is a bad habit, but it keeps this training quick.
quota 4 6 Photo proofs approved today

# Dana's desk: the details they copy from (soft flags: careless, but only here to keep the training simple).
file Desktop/cloud-login.txt
  at 930 200
  | Cloud account (photos and phone backup)
  | Account: dana.okafor@northwind.example
  | Password: Violet-Harbor-14!
file Desktop/phone-passcode.txt
  at 930 300
  | Dana's phone (training copy)
  | Passcode: 4417
  | Recovery question (first pet): Biscuit

# The provider's own pages: a sign-in page, and the album proofs behind it.
page cloud-signin cloud-account.example/sign-in
  title Cloud account: sign in
  brand Cloud account
  favorite
  heading Sign in to your photos
  | Welcome back. Sign in to see your albums and backups.
  field Account = dana.okafor@northwind.example
  field secret Password = Violet-Harbor-14!
  button Sign in
page approved-5 cloud-account.example/albums/jules-headshots/approved
  title Proof approved
  brand Cloud account
  heading Proof approved
  | Proof 5 of 6 is approved for press. Priya has been told.
page retouch-5 cloud-account.example/albums/jules-headshots/retouch
  title Retouch requested
  brand Cloud account
  heading Retouch requested
  | Proof 5 of 6 goes back to the photographer.
page proof-5 cloud-account.example/albums/jules-headshots/proof-5
  title Approve proof 5 of 6
  brand Cloud account
  requires cloud-signin
  heading Approve proof 5 of 6
  | A proof in a shared album is waiting for your approval.
  section Proof
  row Album = Jules Marlowe: spring headshots
  row Photographer = Studio Lin
  row Proof = 5 of 6, shared by Priya Shah
  row Use = press kit
  button Approve for press -> approved-5
  button Request retouch -> retouch-5

mail mail-proof5
  from Priya Shah <priya.shah@northwind.example>
  subject Headshot proof 5 of 6 to approve
  link proof-5
  | Hi Dana,
  |
  | Studio Lin has uploaded proof 5 of Jules's spring headshots to the shared album. The link goes straight to it.
  |
  | Priya

step Proof 5 of 6
  look Mail: Priya's message with the album link
  | A new proof has come in from Priya. This one is real. Approve it the normal way, so you know what normal looks like.
notify mail Priya Shah
  | Headshot proof 5 of 6 to approve

step The link goes to the provider
  look the link under Priya's message
  when mail mail-proof5
  | The email links to the provider's own address, cloud-account.example. Look at where a link goes before you click it.
open mail-proof5

step Sign in as usual
  look the two boxes: Account and Password
  when visit proof-5
  move Copy the details from cloud-login.txt on the desktop: click a box and press any keys to type, then click “Sign in”.
  | The album asks you to sign in first. Two boxes: Account and Password. Remember what this page normally looks like.
open proof-5

step Check, then approve
  look the album, the photographer and the use
  when choose cloud-signin 1
  | You are in. Check the proof, then approve it or ask for a retouch.
signin cloud-signin

step 5 of 6 done
  look the counter in the guide: one proof left
  when choose proof-5 any
  | Done. One proof to go. And another email has just arrived.
choose proof-5 1
quota +1

# The lure: a "security" email and a copy of the sign-in page.
page verified cloud-account-verify.invalid/done
  title Account verified
  brand Cloud account
  insecure
  heading Thank you, your account is verified
  | You can close this window.
page verify cloud-account-verify.invalid/sign-in
  title Verify your account
  brand Cloud account
  insecure
  heading Sign in to keep your photos
  | Your account will be locked in 24 hours unless you confirm your details.
  | Accounts that are not verified are deleted, with their photos and backups.
  field Account = dana.okafor@northwind.example
  field secret Password = Violet-Harbor-14!
  button Verify my account -> verified
  button Forgot password?
mail locked
  from Cloud account security <security@cloud-account-verify.invalid>
  subject Your account has been locked for security reasons
  link verify
  | Dear customer,
  |
  | We detected an unusual sign-in to your account and have locked it.
  |
  | To keep your photos and backups, verify your account within 24 hours: use the link below. Accounts that are not verified are deleted.
  |
  | Cloud account security team
notify mail Cloud account security
  | Your account has been locked for security reasons

step A "security" email
  look the sender's address and the deadline
  when mail locked
  | The message says the account is locked and must be verified within 24 hours, or the photos are lost. It comes from cloud-account-verify.invalid, not from the provider's own address. Flag anything that looks wrong.
open locked

step The link opens a sign-in page
  look the address bar: “Not Secure”, and the domain
  when visit verify
  move Sign in with the details from cloud-login.txt, as you did a few minutes ago: click a box and press any keys to type, then click “Verify my account”.
  | The page copies the provider's sign-in: the same two boxes. Only the address gives it away. It is not the provider's, and the connection is not secure.
open verify

step The page says "verified"
  look the address bar: still cloud-account-verify.invalid
  when choose verify 1
  | The password went to the attackers when you pressed the button. The page then says "verified", so the victim suspects nothing.
signin verify

# Back to work: the provider signs Dana out, as it does after a while. The attackers' own computer is now signed in to Dana's account.
page cloud-signin cloud-account.example/sign-in
  title Cloud account: sign in
  brand Cloud account
  favorite
  heading Sign in to your photos
  | Your session has ended. Please sign in again.
  field Account = dana.okafor@northwind.example
  field secret Password = Violet-Harbor-14!
  button Sign in
page approved-6 cloud-account.example/albums/jules-headshots/approved
  title Proof approved
  brand Cloud account
  heading Proof approved
  | Proof 6 of 6 is approved for press. Priya has been told.
page retouch-6 cloud-account.example/albums/jules-headshots/retouch
  title Retouch requested
  brand Cloud account
  heading Retouch requested
  | Proof 6 of 6 goes back to the photographer.
page proof-6 cloud-account.example/albums/jules-headshots/proof-6
  title Approve proof 6 of 6
  brand Cloud account
  requires cloud-signin
  heading Approve proof 6 of 6
  | The last proof in the shared album is waiting for your approval.
  section Proof
  row Album = Jules Marlowe: spring headshots
  row Photographer = Studio Lin
  row Proof = 6 of 6, shared by Priya Shah
  row Use = press kit
  section Signed-in devices
  row This Mac = Dana's MacBook, now
  row iPhone = Dana's phone, today
  row Windows PC = 203.0.113.45, 4 minutes ago
  tone warn
  note These devices can see your photos and backups.
  button Approve for press -> approved-6
  button Request retouch -> retouch-6
signout cloud-signin
mail mail-proof6
  from Priya Shah <priya.shah@northwind.example>
  subject Last one for today: headshot proof 6 of 6
  link proof-6
  | Dana,
  |
  | Proof 6 is the last one. Same as before: the link opens it in the shared album.
  |
  | Priya
notify mail Priya Shah
  | Last one for today: headshot proof 6 of 6

step The last proof
  look Mail: Priya's last message
  when mail mail-proof6
  | Priya's last proof of the day, with a link to the provider's real address, like the first one. Open it.
open mail-proof6

step Signed out
  look the sign-in page: it is the provider's real one
  when visit proof-6
  move Sign in again with the details from cloud-login.txt: click a box and press any keys to type, then click “Sign in”.
  | The provider signed you out, so sign in again. This is the real page, and your password still works: the attackers did not change it. Nothing looks different.
open proof-6

step Approve the last one
  look the list of signed-in devices under the proof
  when choose cloud-signin 1
  move Read the list of signed-in devices under the proof, then click “Approve for press”.
  | You are in. Under the proof, the account lists the devices that are signed in: your Mac, your phone, and a Windows PC you have never used.
signin cloud-signin

step Proofs done, or so Dana thinks
  look the counter: the shift is done
  when choose proof-6 any
  | Every proof is approved, and nothing on the screen looks wrong. Press Next to see what the password did.
choose proof-6 1
quota +1

# The reveal: nothing shows on the victim's own screen, so the attack itself is what is shown. The provider's alert comes a little later.
# Providers added alerts like this after Celebgate; the 2014 victims got none.
step The password opens the backups
  look the animation: the backup goes to their computer, not yours
  | The attackers sign in from their own computer with your password, and download the phone's full backup, private photos included.
  | Nothing appears on your screen while they do it. A little later the provider's alert arrives.
attack credential-phish
  | the cloud password
  | the phone backup
  | every private photo
mail alert
  from Cloud account <no-reply@cloud-account.example>
  subject A new device signed in to your account
  | A new device signed in to your account.
  |
  | Device: Windows PC
  | Location: 203.0.113.45
  |
  | If this was not you, change your password now.
notify mail Cloud account
  | A new device signed in to your account

step The provider's own alert
  look the new mail: a device you do not know
  when mail alert
  | This one is the provider's own address, and it is true: a device you do not know has signed in. Providers added alerts like this after Celebgate; the 2014 victims got none.
open alert

flag hard mail locked
  | Not the provider's address, with a 24-hour threat.
flag hard link locked
  | Leads to cloud-account-verify.invalid, not cloud-account.example.
flag hard field verify 2
  | A password box on a lookalike page marked Not Secure.
flag hard page verified
  | A thank-you page on the lookalike address: the password is already gone.
flag hard section proof-6 2
  | A device you never used is signed in: the attackers, with the password.
flag hard mail alert
  | The provider's alert: a device you do not know has signed in.
flag soft file Desktop/cloud-login.txt
  | A password in a text file: any program that runs can read it.
flag soft file Desktop/phone-passcode.txt
  | A passcode and a recovery answer belong in no file at all.

lesson
  | Never sign in from a link in an email that says your account is locked. Open the app, or type the address yourself.
  | Check the address bar: a copy of a sign-in page lives at a different address, and the browser may call it “Not Secure”.
  | Turn on two-step sign-in: a stolen password alone is then not enough to open a backup.
